$ jailops app new memcached --dir <dir>/apps
! already_exists: <dir>/apps/memcached.yaml exists
! hint: keep it, or write over it with --force
[exit 5]

$ jailops app new memcached --package memcached,libevent --port 11211 --port 11211/udp --dir <dir>/apps --force
Wrote <dir>/apps/memcached.yaml with 11 line(s) marked TODO, and <dir>/apps/memcached.svg (there already).
Next:
  1. Fill in each line marked TODO; 'jailops app validate <dir>/apps/memcached.yaml' lists the ones left.
  2. On a FreeBSD host, copy both files into /usr/local/etc/jailops/apps and run 'jailops app install memcached'.
  3. Send them to the packages repository (main/jailops-apps/apps/): docs/apps.md, "Write your own app".

